---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base title="How we pick" description="How Stylodex chooses and checks every brand on its lists." canonical="/how-we-pick">
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-14 leading-relaxed">
    <p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
    <h1 class="mt-3 text-4xl font-normal tracking-tight">How we pick</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg">
      A brand appears on a Stylodex list only when it passes every one of these checks. If it stops passing, it comes off the
      list and the count in the title changes with it.
    </p>
    <ol class="mt-8 list-decimal space-y-4 pl-5">
      <li>It is live and selling today, checked against its own store.</li>
      <li>It sells the category the list is about: denim for a list about Levi's, not stationery.</li>
      <li>Its prices come from its own store, in US dollars. If it's cheaper or pricier than the original, we say so.</li>
      <li>Sources outside Stylodex recommend it alongside the original brand, and we keep a record of where.</li>
      <li>There is a specific, checkable reason it belongs on the list.</li>
      <li>All of this has been re-checked in the last 90 days.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-6">
      Some lists are for stores that have closed. The closed store is only the starting point: every store we suggest instead
      is open and passes the same checks.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-8">
      We earn a commission from some links. That never decides what's listed or in what order; see our
      <a href="/disclosure" class="underline">affiliate disclosure</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
